Idle frames: hidden ProgressBar stops repainting; a relaunched window keeps its place; invalidate census names layout requests

ProgressBar: the indeterminate tick (20 Hz) invalidated even when the bar was hidden (GONE/INVISIBLE itself or under a hidden ancestor, alpha 0, or scrolled out of the window), which repainted the whole window: measured on Instagram's profile, ~20 frames/s with nothing moving, main thread ~19%. It now invalidates only when shown with a visible rect, as AOSP animates only while visible. Profile idle: 225 -> 290 of 300 vsyncs skipped, process CPU 20% -> 13% (10% with MACAPK_FRAMESPEED_HEARTBEAT=1, 298/300 skipped).

CocoaShowWindow: an activity relaunch (rotation, configuration change) re-shows the same window. A window already on screen keeps its place in the window order and takes focus only if the app is active; before, MACAPK_NO_ACTIVATE ordered it behind every window on each rotation and the normal path activated the app over whatever was in front. Injector verb `rotate` (View > Girar).

MACAPK_TRACE_INVALIDATE now also counts scheduleLayout ("layout" vs "draw"), and MACAPK_TRACE_INVALIDATE_STACK=<substring of the census key> prints three full stacks of that source after 30 s.

